From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:50:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: keep a DFS channel available until START_AP

A DFS channel stays available for a grace period after its AP stops, so
that the AP can restart without a new CAC. hostapd sets the channel with
NL80211_CMD_SET_WIPHY and sends START_AP once the rest of the BSS is set
up. If the grace period ends between the two, START_AP fails with
-EINVAL and the interface stays disabled until the next restart.

Count the grace period again from the request that sets the channel.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -4188,6 +4188,8 @@
 		if (!cfg80211_reg_can_beacon_relax(&rdev->wiphy, &chandef,
 						   iftype))
 			return -EINVAL;
+		/* a DFS channel must stay available until START_AP */
+		cfg80211_update_last_available(&rdev->wiphy, &chandef);
 		if (wdev->links[link_id].ap.beacon_interval) {
 			struct ieee80211_channel *cur_chan;
 
